  "reading": {
   "title": "Hafsa visits a classroom",
   "text": "Today Hafsa visits Lincoln Elementary School. She wants to work as a substitute teacher, so she wants to see a real classroom.\n\nMs. Carter, a fourth-grade teacher, shows her the room. There are twenty-two desks and a big whiteboard. At nine o'clock the students come in. Ms. Carter says, \"Good morning, class. Sit down, please. Open your notebooks.\" The students are quiet and listen. Then she says, \"Don't talk, please. Look at the board.\"\n\nAfter class, Ms. Carter asks, \"Can you use a computer, Hafsa?\" Hafsa smiles. \"Yes, I can. I can also help children read. I can't drive a school bus, but I can learn!\" Ms. Carter laughs. \"That is fine. You can come back next week.\"",
   "glossary": [
    {
     "en": "substitute teacher",
     "tr": "vekil öğretmen"
    },
    {
     "en": "fourth-grade",
     "tr": "dördüncü sınıf"
    },
    {
     "en": "come back",
     "tr": "geri gelmek"
    },
    {
     "en": "learn",
     "tr": "öğrenmek"
    }
   ],
